// =============================================================================
// 20-apim-403-triage.kql
// The highest-value single diagnostic in this package.
// Answers one question: did APIM reject the request, or did Azure AI Search?
// =============================================================================
//
// RUN THE DISCOVERY QUERIES FIRST
//   00-discover-dependency-types.kql and 01-discover-search-diagnostic-shape.kql.
//   This query itself uses only verified ApiManagementGatewayLogs columns, so it
//   is the most schema-stable file in the library, but the discovery results
//   tell you which correlation keys are available for the follow-up drill-down.
//
// PURPOSE
//   Attribute every 403 seen in the APIM gateway logs to one of three origins,
//   then group the result by the APIM error metadata so the specific policy or
//   backend failure is named rather than guessed.
//
// THE DISTINCTION THAT MAKES THIS QUERY WORK
//   ResponseCode        is what APIM returned TO Copilot Studio.
//   BackendResponseCode is what Azure AI Search returned TO APIM.
//   Divergence between the two is the definitive attribution:
//     BackendResponseCode == 403
//         Search itself rejected the call. This is an authorization or network
//         policy denial: a missing or scoped-out RBAC assignment, key-based auth
//         disabled, or an IP firewall allow-list that no longer covers the
//         connector egress prefixes. Azure AI Search does NOT return 403 for
//         quota and does NOT return 403 for storage exhaustion, so those
//         explanations are off the table.
//     ResponseCode == 403 with no backend code
//         APIM short-circuited before ever calling Search. The only APIM
//         throttling policy that returns 403 is quota or quota-by-key;
//         rate-limit returns 429. An ip-filter denial also lands here, as does
//         a validate-jwt or check-header rejection. A missing or invalid APIM
//         subscription key returns 401, not 403, which rules that out.
//     Both set but different
//         APIM rewrote the status, so read LastErrorSource before concluding
//         anything about the backend.
//   Branching on this collapses roughly thirteen candidate causes to about four.
//   Research: .copilot-tracking/research/2026-09-22/ai-search-scaling-206-403-rca-research.md
//             Lines 312-336 (Q8c and the ResponseCode explanation),
//             Lines 142-163 (D6 ranked hypotheses 1 through 5)
//
// TARGET TABLE
//   ApiManagementGatewayLogs. All columns used below are verified against the
//   published table reference.
//
// PREREQUISITES
//   * The GatewayLogs diagnostic category enabled on the APIM service and sent
//     to this Log Analytics workspace.
//   * APIM must NOT be on the Consumption tier. Consumption supports no resource
//     logs at all, which would invalidate this entire diagnostic path. Confirm
//     the tier before planning around gateway logs (open item U9).
//   Enable with: scripts/Enable-DiagnosticSettings.ps1
//   Audit policies with: scripts/Get-ApimPolicyAudit.ps1
//
// HEALTHY VS UNHEALTHY
//   Healthy   : zero rows over the window.
//   Result A  : "403 from Azure AI Search backend" dominates. Go to Search-side
//               authorization: check networkRuleSet.ipRules against the current
//               AzureConnectors service tags for the region, check RBAC role
//               assignments per index, and check whether key-based auth is
//               disabled. Then run 22-connector-403-by-index.kql.
//   Result B  : "403 raised by APIM policy" dominates. Go to the policy XML at
//               all four scopes and look for quota, quota-by-key, and ip-filter.
//               LastErrorReason usually names it outright: CallerIpNotAllowed,
//               CallerIpBlocked, or a quota message.
//   Result C  : mixed. Two independent causes are running concurrently. Split
//               the investigation by Origin403 and treat them separately.
//
// Derived from Q8c-Apim403Triage,
//   .copilot-tracking/research/2026-09-22/ai-search-scaling-206-403-rca-research.md Lines 314-334
// =============================================================================

let lookback = 7d;
ApiManagementGatewayLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
| where ResponseCode == 403 or BackendResponseCode == 403
| extend Origin403 = case(
      BackendResponseCode == 403, "403 from Azure AI Search backend",
      ResponseCode == 403 and (isnull(BackendResponseCode) or BackendResponseCode == 0), "403 raised by APIM policy",
      "403 rewritten by APIM")
| summarize
    Count         = count(),
    FirstSeen     = min(TimeGenerated),
    LastSeen      = max(TimeGenerated),
    Apis          = make_set(ApiId, 10),
    Operations    = make_set(OperationName, 10),
    Subscriptions = make_set(ApimSubscriptionId, 10),
    CallerIps     = make_set(CallerIpAddress, 10),
    SampleBackend = take_any(BackendUrl),
    SampleMessage = take_any(LastErrorMessage)
    by Origin403, LastErrorSource, LastErrorReason, LastErrorScope, LastErrorSection
| order by Count desc

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// COMPANION A: the full outcome attribution, not just 403
// Run this when the 403 picture is clean but calls are still failing. It catches
// APIM post-processing failures, where the backend succeeded and APIM still
// returned an error.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// let lookback = 24h;
// ApiManagementGatewayLogs
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
// | where ResponseCode >= 400 or BackendResponseCode >= 400 or IsRequestSuccess == false
// | extend Attribution = case(
//       ResponseCode >= 400 and (isnull(BackendResponseCode) or BackendResponseCode == 0), "APIM-generated (no backend call)",
//       BackendResponseCode >= 400 and ResponseCode == BackendResponseCode,                "Backend error (passed through)",
//       BackendResponseCode >= 400 and ResponseCode != BackendResponseCode,                "Backend error (rewritten by APIM)",
//       BackendResponseCode  < 400 and ResponseCode >= 400,                                "APIM post-processing failure",
//       "Other")
// | summarize
//     Requests       = count(),
//     DistinctApis   = dcount(ApiId),
//     AvgBackendMs   = round(avg(BackendTime), 1),
//     P95TotalMs     = round(percentile(TotalTime, 95), 1),
//     SampleErrorMsg = take_any(LastErrorMessage)
//     by Attribution, ResponseCode, BackendResponseCode, LastErrorSource, LastErrorReason
// | order by Requests desc

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// COMPANION B: attribution over time
// Shows whether the 403s are a continuous condition or a burst that correlates
// with load. Bursty and load-correlated points at an APIM quota policy; flat and
// continuous points at a firewall or RBAC change.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// let lookback = 7d;
// ApiManagementGatewayLogs
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
// | extend Attribution = case(
//       ResponseCode < 400 and (BackendResponseCode < 400 or isnull(BackendResponseCode)), "Success",
//       ResponseCode >= 400 and (isnull(BackendResponseCode) or BackendResponseCode == 0),  "APIM-generated",
//       BackendResponseCode >= 400,                                                         "Backend (Azure AI Search)",
//       "APIM post-processing")
// | summarize Requests = count() by Attribution, bin(TimeGenerated, 5m)
// | render timechart with (title = "APIM request outcome attribution")

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// COMPANION C: raw rows for correlation
// CorrelationId is the candidate join key back to the Copilot Studio connector
// span. It is UNVERIFIED that APIM propagates it to or from that span, so run
// this to test whether the identifiers ever line up before designing around it.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// let lookback = 24h;
// ApiManagementGatewayLogs
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
// | where ResponseCode == 403 or BackendResponseCode == 403
// | project TimeGenerated, CorrelationId, ApiId, OperationName, ResponseCode, BackendResponseCode,
//           LastErrorSource, LastErrorReason, LastErrorMessage, CallerIpAddress, BackendUrl, TotalTime, BackendTime
// | order by TimeGenerated desc
// | take 100
